WEBVTT

00:02.600 --> 00:05.100
Zakishino! Is Akina-san around?

00:04.020 --> 00:07.980
m 0 0 l 180 0 l 180 90 l 0 90

00:04.020 --> 00:07.980
<b>Public Relations
Yamagishi Yuusuke
(First year at the company)</b>

00:05.100 --> 00:07.980
Would it kill you to be 
a little more professional?

00:08.500 --> 00:10.240
And who's Akina-san?

00:10.240 --> 00:12.720
That'd be me! Akina Chihiro.

00:12.720 --> 00:15.160
Oh, Manager! Sorry about that.

00:15.470 --> 00:17.780
Shinozaki-kun, is Katase-san around?

00:17.780 --> 00:20.750
She just stepped out.

00:20.750 --> 00:24.430
Oh, so you remember <i>her</i> name, huh?

00:24.430 --> 00:26.540
I mean, she's my immediate senior!

00:28.790 --> 00:33.040
Zakishino... were you aware 
that it's Tuesday, bro?

00:33.040 --> 00:34.050
Yeah, I was.

00:34.050 --> 00:36.950
It's still the weekend in my heart, though.

00:37.800 --> 00:42.310
<b>Tuesday</b>

00:37.800 --> 00:42.310
<b>Weekend</b>

00:37.800 --> 00:42.310
I'm in the arms of Tuesday, 
while dreaming of the distant weekend...

00:42.310 --> 00:45.440
It doesn't matter how you dress it up. 
It's still only Tuesday.

00:47.120 --> 00:50.200
Stop being stupid and get to work.

00:51.780 --> 00:54.830
Cool as ice, like always, Hayakawa-san.

00:55.200 --> 00:59.100
Zakishino, this is gonna be a long week!

00:59.100 --> 01:01.850
It's the same length as it was last week.

01:01.850 --> 01:04.210
I'm talking experientially, bro!

01:04.210 --> 01:05.870
Shinozaki-san!

01:05.870 --> 01:06.710
Senpai?

01:06.710 --> 01:08.960
What do you want to do for lunch today?

01:08.960 --> 01:12.160
Sorry, I made plans to eat with Yamagishi-kun.

01:09.560 --> 01:10.870
<i>Such a cutie!</i>

01:12.160 --> 01:13.210
I see.

01:13.210 --> 01:15.780
Next time, then!

01:18.040 --> 01:19.220
Step, step, step...

01:19.220 --> 01:22.440
I think I'm good with this being a long week.

01:23.120 --> 01:24.500
Damn, man!

01:36.950 --> 01:41.710
My Tiny Senpai

02:54.980 --> 02:59.990
#03 Is This How I Look to You?

02:58.530 --> 02:59.390
Shinozaki-kun!

02:59.390 --> 03:00.200
Yes, sir?!

03:01.030 --> 03:03.050
Care to join me for lunch?

03:04.120 --> 03:06.200
<i>The boss where I work...</i>

03:06.780 --> 03:09.220
<i>is someone I truly don't understand.</i>

03:10.580 --> 03:12.710
So, how's work going?

03:12.710 --> 03:16.960
Thanks to Senpai's help, 
it's been a lot of fun.

03:16.960 --> 03:18.600
That's good to hear.

03:19.140 --> 03:21.470
We have a hard time getting new personnel,

03:21.880 --> 03:26.850
so when you were hired, Katase-san 
was so excited, she became a handful.

03:27.150 --> 03:28.280
She was?

03:28.280 --> 03:29.350
Indeed she was.

03:29.680 --> 03:32.350
I remember it like it was yesterday...

03:33.460 --> 03:36.840
I'm thinking of interviewing this one.

03:36.840 --> 03:39.610
Is it a boy or a girl?

03:40.280 --> 03:43.470
Interview's all done. 
He seems nice, so it's a done deal.

03:43.470 --> 03:46.270
When's he coming? When are you expecting?

03:46.270 --> 03:49.870
At the time I wondered, 
"Huh? Am I having a baby?"

03:50.240 --> 03:51.100
My son.

03:51.100 --> 03:52.400
I'm sorry, who?

03:52.400 --> 03:53.470
Manager...

03:54.610 --> 03:58.120
Could you not tell Shinozaki-san 
these weird stories?

03:58.120 --> 03:59.260
Senpai?

03:59.260 --> 04:02.890
Excuse me, could I get the tuna and 
mushroom Arrabbiata, and the shrimp...

04:02.890 --> 04:05.050
Are you listening to me?!

04:05.050 --> 04:06.640
Why, of course I am.

04:07.890 --> 04:09.600
She's cute when she's mad, too, isn't she?

04:09.600 --> 04:11.560
Er, uh, yes. She is—

04:11.560 --> 04:13.640
Please don't make him say that!

04:13.950 --> 04:18.640
Now, now.... Since you're here, 
Katase-san, why don't you join us?

04:18.640 --> 04:20.150
O-Okay.

04:20.750 --> 04:23.180
Have to say, it's nostalgic to think about.

04:23.180 --> 04:26.890
Do you remember when 
Shinozaki-kun first joined up?

04:26.890 --> 04:30.160
I mean, it wasn't really that long ago...

04:30.540 --> 04:33.630
I suppose you're right! 
It was just a while back.

04:33.630 --> 04:37.170
Are we still talking about this?! 
It's ancient news!

04:37.910 --> 04:42.060
My name is Shinozaki Takuma, 
and I'll be working here starting today.

04:42.060 --> 04:43.550
It's nice to meet all of you!

04:43.550 --> 04:45.820
I'm Akina, your manager.
Nice to meet you.

04:45.820 --> 04:49.290
Yes, sir! Thanks in advance for your guidance!

04:49.290 --> 04:51.310
It's a pleasure to be working for you!

04:51.800 --> 04:53.650
This is Katase-san.

04:53.650 --> 04:57.610
You'll be sitting next to her, 
so if you have questions, she'll help you.

04:58.560 --> 05:02.700
I'm Katase. If you need to 
know anything, just ask.

05:02.700 --> 05:04.570
<i>So tiny! And cute!</i>

05:04.570 --> 05:06.820
A kohai! I got a kohai!

05:05.570 --> 05:08.460
<i>What is this fluttery, little creature?!</i>

05:07.700 --> 05:09.800
A kohai, a kohai!

05:08.460 --> 05:10.580
<i>I can't believe my seat 
gets such benefits...</i>

05:10.580 --> 05:12.040
Someone's excited!

05:13.000 --> 05:15.610
Please, Manager, cut that out!

05:16.450 --> 05:18.080
<i>Heartwarming...</i>

05:18.490 --> 05:21.710
Let's start with getting your PC set up.

05:21.710 --> 05:22.840
Right.

05:23.180 --> 05:25.470
<i>This company seems great.</i>

05:25.940 --> 05:28.260
<i>I get a feeling this job will be fun.</i>

05:30.630 --> 05:32.470
<i>She's staring a hole in me!</i>

05:32.800 --> 05:35.100
<i>It's a gaze that won't let 
a single mistake slip by...</i>

05:35.100 --> 05:37.980
<i>not of concern, but of oversight!</i>

05:37.980 --> 05:39.360
<i>Wait...</i>

05:39.360 --> 05:41.850
<i>Could that friendly act 
from earlier be a facade</i>

05:41.850 --> 05:45.200
<i>to get my to lower my guard 
before they harshly evaluate me?!</i>

05:45.200 --> 05:46.490
I dunno about this one.

05:46.490 --> 05:47.740
You don't, eh?

05:47.740 --> 05:50.430
<i>In that case, I better stay on my toes!</i>

05:50.430 --> 05:53.850
<i>Maybe I can't make a good impression,
but I can at least avoid a bad one!</i>

05:56.750 --> 05:59.250
<i>Her gaze is getting even more intense!</i>

06:01.220 --> 06:02.000
<i>Huh?</i>

06:02.000 --> 06:04.380
Log in

06:02.000 --> 06:04.380
Network ID Information
Please enter your password in order to verify your access

06:02.000 --> 06:04.380
Password

06:02.000 --> 06:04.380
Cancel

06:02.300 --> 06:03.980
<i>A network password?</i>

06:04.940 --> 06:07.980
<i>I don't think I mixed up the procedure...</i>

06:07.980 --> 06:10.910
<i>And I've got all the paperwork 
I was given here.</i>

06:10.910 --> 06:11.850
<i>Which leaves...</i>

06:12.550 --> 06:17.480
<i>I should probably ask about this, 
but what if I get the timing wrong?</i>

06:18.020 --> 06:19.130
<i>If I'm too fast...</i>

06:18.020 --> 06:22.980
m 0 0 l 68 0 l 68 130 l 0 130

06:18.020 --> 06:22.980
<b>Too
fast</b>

06:20.150 --> 06:22.940
Are you really asking without 
actually looking into the issue?

06:22.980 --> 06:28.740
m 0 0 l 68 0 l 68 130 l 0 130

06:22.980 --> 06:28.740
<b>Too
Slow</b>

06:23.300 --> 06:24.590
<i>If I take too long...</i>

06:24.590 --> 06:28.740
Why didn't you ask sooner? You wasted time.

06:29.200 --> 06:30.360
<i>Which is it?!</i>

06:30.690 --> 06:33.560
<i>For now, I should check the guidelines again...</i>

06:35.260 --> 06:39.360
For the network password, it's your branch 
name and then your employee ID number.

06:39.360 --> 06:41.640
Th-Thank you...

06:42.500 --> 06:46.760
You were totally intimidated by 
Katase-san at first, weren't you?

06:46.760 --> 06:50.330
It's more like... I was getting nervous
and freaking out a bit.

06:50.330 --> 06:52.760
It was the same for me.

06:53.460 --> 06:55.260
<i>Staaare...</i>

06:55.710 --> 06:57.180
<i>Shinozaki-san.</i>

06:57.770 --> 07:00.170
<i>Is there anything you don't understand?</i>

07:00.170 --> 07:04.270
<i>You can ask me about it, y'know? 
I'm just waiting to be helpful!</i>

07:04.700 --> 07:05.400
<i>Glance.</i>

07:05.400 --> 07:08.860
<i>But I can't! Manager will make fun 
of me for making a fuss again...</i>

07:08.860 --> 07:12.620
<i>Just stay focused and 
keep from grinning too much...</i>

07:13.440 --> 07:15.490
<i>He seems to be having some trouble.</i>

07:15.740 --> 07:18.020
<i>This looks like a job for his senpai!</i>

07:19.030 --> 07:23.110
For the network password, it's your branch 
name and then your employee ID number.

07:23.110 --> 07:25.290
Th-Thank you...

07:26.570 --> 07:29.740
Oh, sorry, I shouldn't impose.

07:29.740 --> 07:32.840
No, it's okay.
 I should've been the one to ask.

07:32.840 --> 07:36.100
But really, if you have 
questions, don't hesitate.

07:36.100 --> 07:37.080
Sure!

07:37.960 --> 07:40.250
<i>She really was worried...</i>

07:41.280 --> 07:43.650
Thanks for your concern, Senpai.

07:46.180 --> 07:50.690
Oh, should I not call you Senpai? Is it 
unprofessional? Too much like a student?

07:50.690 --> 07:56.580
m 0 0 l 90 0 l 90 84 l 0 84

07:50.690 --> 07:56.580
<b>Kohai
Cuteness
Meter</b>

07:56.580 --> 07:57.530
Senpai?

07:57.530 --> 07:58.650
Yes!

07:58.650 --> 07:59.360
Senpai?

07:59.360 --> 08:00.520
Yes, right!

08:00.520 --> 08:01.240
Senpai...?

08:01.240 --> 08:02.580
Yes, that's me, your senpai!

08:04.580 --> 08:07.090
Oh, sorry... it's just...

08:07.090 --> 08:09.790
I'm really excited 
about having my first kohai....

08:09.790 --> 08:12.890
And I've been trying to stay calm, but...

08:12.890 --> 08:16.600
I guess I haven't been 
conducting myself like a senpai.

08:16.600 --> 08:19.930
No! I'm glad if you're glad!

08:20.330 --> 08:24.120
I was also excited about 
meeting my first work senpai, so...

08:25.310 --> 08:29.320
I guess this is a first for both of us, huh?

08:29.660 --> 08:33.200
Well, since we're both new at this, 
let's try our best!

08:33.640 --> 08:35.200
R-Right!

08:37.700 --> 08:39.690
Did I just pick up some lewd vibes...?

08:39.690 --> 08:41.210
You did not!

08:41.700 --> 08:44.220
Ah, that really takes me back!

08:44.220 --> 08:44.960
Huh?

08:45.480 --> 08:46.830
What's wrong, you two?

08:46.830 --> 08:50.040
It's kind of embarrassing to think about...

08:50.040 --> 08:50.960
Agreed.

08:50.960 --> 08:52.200
I see.

08:52.200 --> 08:54.970
Well, to make up for embarrassing you two...

08:55.430 --> 08:58.470
Dessert will be my treat. What would you like?

08:58.750 --> 09:02.220
Really?! Thank you so much!

09:02.220 --> 09:03.930
What should I get...?

09:03.930 --> 09:07.230
Senpai, you let him buy you off 
a little too easily.

09:07.230 --> 09:09.480
Do you not want dessert, Shinozaki-san?

09:09.480 --> 09:12.620
If you don't, I'd be glad to eat yours!

09:12.620 --> 09:14.760
I'll take mine, thanks!

09:14.760 --> 09:15.990
Oh, dear.

09:16.520 --> 09:19.630
Are you ready for tomorrow's meeting?

09:19.630 --> 09:20.560
All set!

09:20.560 --> 09:21.610
Very good!

09:23.140 --> 09:26.340
<i>My Tiny Senpai</i>.

09:28.000 --> 09:30.000
Good work today!

09:30.330 --> 09:34.260
I got super nervous having a 
meeting at another company...

09:34.260 --> 09:36.540
You do, don't you?

09:37.070 --> 09:40.570
It was a huge relief having you backing me up.

09:42.140 --> 09:46.800
Was it a good reminder that I'm your senpai?

09:46.800 --> 09:48.310
It was!

09:48.840 --> 09:52.890
Well, let's head back to the office 
and get back to work!

09:52.890 --> 09:54.150
R-Right!

10:05.890 --> 10:07.500
So cute!

10:07.950 --> 10:09.960
Is it some kind of mascot character?

10:10.330 --> 10:15.210
A kitty with a bunny hoodie, 
and a doggy with a bear hoodie!

10:16.580 --> 10:19.090
<i>Y'know, this stuffed animal...</i>

10:19.530 --> 10:21.950
<i>Something about this stuffed animal...</i>

10:22.350 --> 10:24.920
It reminds me of Senpai.

10:22.350 --> 10:24.920
It reminds me of Shinozaki-san.

10:26.890 --> 10:28.480
You think so...?

10:28.960 --> 10:32.190
Is this how I look to you?

10:32.190 --> 10:35.190
Well, when I say that, I mean...

10:37.940 --> 10:42.620
<i>You can say "You're that cute!" 
It's the perfect time to say it, me!</i>

10:43.410 --> 10:46.370
Y-You are kinda catlike, I'd say...

10:46.770 --> 10:48.930
You really think so?

10:48.930 --> 10:50.750
<i>Extremely feline!</i>

10:50.750 --> 10:54.380
And is this how you see me, Senpai?

10:54.380 --> 10:56.160
That's right.

10:56.160 --> 10:57.500
There's something about his gaze,

10:57.500 --> 11:00.800
and the unique look
of a dog in a bear hoodie...

11:00.800 --> 11:03.550
I dare say he's 90% Shinozaki-san.

11:03.550 --> 11:05.190
Almost 100%?!

11:09.680 --> 11:12.590
Well... would you like me to catch them?

11:12.590 --> 11:14.810
Can you?!

11:14.810 --> 11:15.650
I think so.

11:16.240 --> 11:19.470
When I was in high school, 
I used to spend a lot of time at the arcade,

11:19.470 --> 11:23.590
and I had a pretty decent collection 
of cute plushies like these.

11:24.360 --> 11:27.910
You must like cute things, Shinozaki-san.

11:27.910 --> 11:29.100
I do.

11:29.100 --> 11:31.400
One of the reasons I applied to Sunpick was

11:31.400 --> 11:34.500
because I wanted to be involved in 
making that sort of thing.

11:35.350 --> 11:37.000
I like that.

11:38.480 --> 11:39.920
Cute things, I mean!

11:40.320 --> 11:44.770
<i>I see! That makes sense... 
Got kind of worked up there.</i>

11:44.770 --> 11:46.040
Is something wrong?

11:46.040 --> 11:48.220
Oh, no, nothing.

11:48.820 --> 11:52.730
Our company's character, Meowtaro, 
is cute, too, isn't he?

11:53.160 --> 11:56.750
We had plenty of Meowtaro 
merch at home, too.

11:56.750 --> 11:58.860
My sister is six years older, 
and she loves him.

11:59.180 --> 12:04.110
Me liking cute stuff might be 
her influence, come to think of it.

12:05.730 --> 12:08.620
So you're a big sister's boy, Shinozaki-san?

12:08.620 --> 12:11.830
I dunno if I'd say that.

12:14.020 --> 12:15.780
It's cute.

12:17.160 --> 12:21.380
<i>Y-You're the cute one, Senpai!</i>

12:22.680 --> 12:24.780
Okay, here we go.

12:24.780 --> 12:27.140
Okay. Good luck!

12:29.640 --> 12:33.640
<i>Oh, boy! Oh, boy! Oh, boy! Oh, boy...</i>

12:36.040 --> 12:37.650
<i>Sulk...</i>

12:38.080 --> 12:39.790
That was a close one.

12:39.790 --> 12:42.150
<i>I got more than 
a 100 yen's worth of value, for sure.</i>

12:42.150 --> 12:44.820
I get the feeling I can manage on the next one.

12:44.820 --> 12:46.680
Are you sure?

12:46.680 --> 12:48.990
<i>I want to protect this smile.</i>

12:49.870 --> 12:51.080
<b>Dog</b>

12:49.870 --> 12:51.500
<b>Cat</b>

12:51.500 --> 12:55.530
<i>Oh, boy! Oh, boy! Oh, boy! Oh, boy...</i>

12:59.870 --> 13:02.240
Almost got 'em.

13:02.240 --> 13:04.260
<i>I could watch this all day.</i>

13:04.260 --> 13:07.260
Sorry about that, Senpai. But this time...

13:07.260 --> 13:10.250
Don't worry about it, Shinozaki-san.

13:10.250 --> 13:11.890
Even if you don't manage on the next one...

13:12.250 --> 13:14.480
My budget is 30,000!

13:14.480 --> 13:17.150
<i>The height of a child with 
the purchasing power of an adult!</i>

13:20.430 --> 13:21.900
Is this gonna work...?

13:22.280 --> 13:23.900
Do you think...?

13:27.320 --> 13:29.320
<i>It's caught on the bear.</i>

13:29.320 --> 13:29.950
<i>Buck...</i>

13:31.240 --> 13:32.180
<i>Buck-kaw!</i>

13:35.000 --> 13:37.130
All right!

13:38.340 --> 13:39.930
S-Sorry...

13:39.930 --> 13:41.000
It's fine.

13:41.000 --> 13:44.010
Two at once! Nicely done!

13:44.330 --> 13:47.260
Nah, that was a coincidence.

13:47.860 --> 13:53.010
Maybe the other one was worried 
about being lonely and tagged along.

13:53.010 --> 13:55.420
Th-That might be it.

13:55.420 --> 13:58.270
<i>And you said that one reminded you of me...</i>

13:58.560 --> 14:03.780
In that case, they should 
stay together, so they don't get lonely.

14:04.200 --> 14:05.780
<i>Together...!</i>

14:10.080 --> 14:13.160
<i>She means the stuffed animals! That's all!</i>

14:13.530 --> 14:16.160
Now that we've got them, let's name them!

14:16.160 --> 14:20.420
Since this one's a bear dog 
that looks like Shinozaki-san...

14:20.780 --> 14:21.980
Takuma-kun!

14:21.980 --> 14:23.790
That's kind of on the nose, isn't it?!

14:22.500 --> 14:28.680
<b>Shinozaki           Takuma</b>

14:23.790 --> 14:26.780
Is that bad? 
I like how it has "kuma" like bear.

14:26.780 --> 14:28.680
I didn't say no!

14:29.020 --> 14:30.920
In that case, this one...

14:30.920 --> 14:33.680
Should probably be "Shiori-san," right?

14:34.060 --> 14:35.480
That's fine by me.

14:35.480 --> 14:36.680
It is?!

14:37.620 --> 14:41.340
They'd get along as senpai and kohai, then.

14:41.340 --> 14:43.060
G-Good point...

14:43.390 --> 14:46.350
<i>Something about this is giving me 
butterflies in my tummy...</i>

14:46.350 --> 14:47.690
Shinozaki-san.

14:48.670 --> 14:52.320
Thank you for getting 
these stuffed animals for me.

14:53.520 --> 14:56.580
Were you really that glad about it?

14:56.960 --> 14:58.010
Yes.

15:02.580 --> 15:05.170
This one should probably be 
"Shiori-san", right?

15:08.790 --> 15:11.400
Okay, let's head back to the office!

15:11.400 --> 15:12.220
Right!

15:14.680 --> 15:16.930
<b>Product Development</b>

15:14.680 --> 15:16.930
<b>Group 2</b>

15:14.680 --> 15:17.220
Hayakawa-san, Shinozaki-kun...

15:17.680 --> 15:20.190
Could you come here for a sec?

15:21.810 --> 15:24.440
<b>40th Anniversary</b>

15:22.640 --> 15:24.440
A Meowtaro video game?

15:24.440 --> 15:30.260
Yep. I volunteered to design it, 
and I wanted to get some opinions.

15:30.670 --> 15:32.110
What kind of game is it?

15:32.110 --> 15:34.580
A dating sim.

15:34.580 --> 15:35.990
It's an otome game!

15:39.160 --> 15:41.020
A Meowtaro...

15:41.020 --> 15:42.750
Otome game?

15:43.120 --> 15:46.750
I've got a start menu ready, so take a look

15:47.040 --> 15:47.820
See?

15:49.970 --> 15:54.470
<b>Doki Doki
Meowtaro
</b>~Our Academy of Romance~

15:49.970 --> 15:54.470
Start

15:50.360 --> 15:51.930
Wh-What the...?

15:51.930 --> 15:54.470
Say hello to the anthropomorphized 
hot version of Meowtaro!

15:54.470 --> 15:58.350
The idea is to seize control of 
the latent otome game fan demographic!

15:58.750 --> 16:00.030
Would that work?

16:00.030 --> 16:01.760
I guess it could.

16:01.760 --> 16:03.100
I see...

16:03.100 --> 16:06.350
I'm not sure what fans of 
classic Meowtaro will think of this, though.

16:06.350 --> 16:09.240
I thought you all had gone home. 
What are you doing?

16:09.780 --> 16:12.280
<i>Speaking of classic fans!</i>

16:13.320 --> 16:16.250
Katase-san, I'd love to hear your opinion.

16:16.250 --> 16:17.780
Check out the Meowtaro video game!

16:18.210 --> 16:20.410
A Meowtaro video game?!

16:20.410 --> 16:21.790
Here it is!

16:23.790 --> 16:25.640
What do you think, Katase-san?

16:25.640 --> 16:28.550
It's an otome game featuring 
an anthropomorphized hot version of Meowtaro!

16:28.550 --> 16:30.120
<i>This is Meowtaro...?</i>

16:30.120 --> 16:30.860
<i>Hot?</i>

16:30.860 --> 16:31.740
<i>Anthropomorphized?</i>

16:31.740 --> 16:33.040
<i>And this is Meowtaro...</i>

16:33.040 --> 16:34.300
<i>What in the world...?</i>

16:36.600 --> 16:39.310
Senpai's neural circuits have shorted out!

16:39.940 --> 16:44.310
Now, what I really wanted to ask you about 
are some romantic anecdotes.

16:44.840 --> 16:46.440
Romantic anecdotes?

16:46.440 --> 16:51.370
Remember, this is a Meowtaro dating sim.

16:51.370 --> 16:56.200
So I was hoping to hear about all kinds of 
romantic stories, for reference!

16:56.200 --> 16:59.620
R-Romantic anecdotes, huh...?

16:58.240 --> 17:00.410
m 0 0 l 195 0 l 195 84 l 0 84

16:58.240 --> 17:00.410
<b>Never had a
boyfriend</b>

17:00.560 --> 17:03.340
Th-This is kind of sudden...

17:02.120 --> 17:04.210
m 0 0 l 195 0 l 195 84 l 0 84

17:02.120 --> 17:04.210
<b>Never had a
girlfriend</b>

17:04.040 --> 17:08.330
Y-Yeah. It's hard to 
think of anything that'd help...

17:05.250 --> 17:08.330
m 0 0 l 195 0 l 195 84 l 0 84

17:05.250 --> 17:08.330
<b>Never had a
boyfriend</b>

17:08.330 --> 17:11.840
<b>Total Romantic Experience: Zero</b>

17:08.720 --> 17:11.530
Wait, have none of you been 
in a relationship before?

17:11.840 --> 17:12.590
<b>Bingo</b>

17:12.960 --> 17:16.840
C-Come to think of it, Hayakawa, 
when you were interviewing for Sunpick,

17:16.840 --> 17:19.880
didn't you say you ran into Prince Charming?

17:19.880 --> 17:22.470
You wanna talk about that <i>now</i>?!

17:22.470 --> 17:25.340
What is that all about?! Spill the details!

17:27.680 --> 17:30.860
Well... it wasn't that big of a deal.

17:30.900 --> 17:35.110
<b>Sunpick Ltd.
Interview Venue</b>

17:36.320 --> 17:40.120
<i>I can't believe this happened 
right before an important interview...</i>

17:40.560 --> 17:42.120
<i>I really screwed up...</i>

17:42.400 --> 17:43.820
<i>What now?</i>

17:43.820 --> 17:45.660
Are you all right?

17:48.800 --> 17:50.250
You've got an interview, right?

17:50.250 --> 17:52.040
Y-Yes...

17:52.710 --> 17:53.780
One second.

17:55.840 --> 17:57.290
There you go.

17:57.290 --> 17:59.260
Thank you very much.

17:59.260 --> 18:02.490
It'll be a while 
until it dries completely, but...

18:02.490 --> 18:03.600
Try it on.

18:04.920 --> 18:06.600
O-Okay.

18:12.540 --> 18:14.710
Good luck with the interview.

18:16.490 --> 18:19.110
R-Right...

18:19.840 --> 18:20.890
Be seeing you.

18:24.420 --> 18:26.550
<i>Does he work at Sunpick...?</i>

18:29.920 --> 18:31.760
Could the next interviewee please come in?

18:31.760 --> 18:32.630
Coming!

18:33.830 --> 18:36.250
<i>I wonder if I'll see him again 
if I get the job...</i>

18:36.630 --> 18:38.680
<i>No, not now!</i>

18:38.680 --> 18:40.760
<i>I need to focus on the interview!</i>

18:42.210 --> 18:43.260
Pardon me.

18:46.130 --> 18:49.700
My name is Hayakawa Chinatsu. 
Thank you for your time today.

18:54.850 --> 18:58.360
So the person who helped you was one of 
the people conducting the interview?

18:58.360 --> 19:01.630
That feels an awful lot like fate!

19:01.630 --> 19:04.960
Who was it, anyway? Did you 
see him again after getting the job?

19:05.370 --> 19:08.870
W-Well, I did, but...

19:12.690 --> 19:14.140
The thing about fireworks is...

19:14.140 --> 19:16.750
they're pretty because 
you see them at a distance.

19:17.410 --> 19:19.260
She got weirdly philosophical about it!

19:19.260 --> 19:24.280
Never mind that! I told one, 
so you need to, too, Yamagishi-san!

19:24.280 --> 19:26.010
Me?! I...

19:26.010 --> 19:30.890
I mean, obviously I don't have any! 
That's the whole reason I'm asking!

19:31.540 --> 19:33.770
The way you believe me is kind of depressing...

19:36.020 --> 19:38.500
Romantic anecdotes...

19:45.490 --> 19:48.960
Since this one's a bear dog 
that looks like Shinozaki-san...

19:48.960 --> 19:50.160
Takuma-kun!

19:50.160 --> 19:55.120
<i>I can't believe I said that, much less 
that I'm thinking about it now.</i>

19:55.120 --> 19:58.550
<i>I'm so embarrassed about 
what I said, in hindsight.</i>

19:59.920 --> 20:04.520
Still, it's just a stuffed animal. It has 
nothing to do with the real Shinozaki-san.

20:06.390 --> 20:08.810
Wait, didn't I have a...

20:09.750 --> 20:11.160
Ta-da!

20:11.160 --> 20:13.440
I added a necktie.

20:13.440 --> 20:15.770
Pretty good if I say so myself.

20:16.400 --> 20:19.150
Why am I making the resemblance even stronger?!

20:19.150 --> 20:21.390
I need to calm down.

20:21.390 --> 20:22.650
It's just a stuffed animal.

20:22.970 --> 20:24.660
Just a stuffed...

20:32.410 --> 20:35.670
Stuffed animal! It's just a stuffed animal!

20:48.020 --> 20:52.180
Maybe I should rearrange them 
so he's out of sight...

20:54.820 --> 20:57.850
Shiori-san's on top of Takuma-kun!

21:00.610 --> 21:02.080
Shiori-san...

21:03.890 --> 21:05.420
Takuma-kun...

21:09.950 --> 21:12.950
Shiori-san! You can't!

21:26.040 --> 21:28.260
Shiori-san and Takuma-kun.

21:28.920 --> 21:32.250
A senpai and a kohai who get along!
